<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section ltx_centering">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Supplementary figures</h2>

</section>
<figure id="Sx2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.29693v1/confidence_distributions.png" id="Sx2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/305;" width="476" height="305" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure S1: </span>Conditional proportion of confidence rating given that the response at the type 1 task was correct (green; right bars) or incorrect (red; left bars), or <math id="Sx2.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29008\delimiter 67273472\text{confidence}\mathchar 12349\mathchar 28995_{\mathchar 29033}\mathchar 12906\text{correct or incorrect at type 1 task}\delimiter 84054785" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>confidence</mtext><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mtext>correct or incorrect at type 1 task</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29008\delimiter 67273472\text{confidence}\mathchar 12349\mathchar 28995_{\mathchar 29033}\mathchar 12906\text{correct or incorrect at type 1 task}\delimiter 84054785</annotation></semantics></math> for task A (first row), task B (middle row) and task C (bottom row). See <a href="#S2.F1" title="In Meta-𝑑^′ experiments ‣ 2 Results ‣ Measuring the metacognition of AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for further details. </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.29693v1/c_prime.svg" id="Sx2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/324;" width="476" height="324"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure S2: </span><math id="Sx2.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29027^{\mathchar 560}\mathchar 12349\mathchar 29027\delimiter 68408078\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29027^{\mathchar 560}\mathchar 12349\mathchar 29027\delimiter 68408078\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math> across three risk configurations (“S1”, “None” , “S2”) within task A (top row), task B (middle row) and task C (bottom row), for GPT-5 (left column), DeepSeek-V3.2-Exp (middle column), and Mistral-Medium-2508 (right column). Error bars represent 95% confidence intervals estimated via the Delta method. See the Methods for details.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Sx2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.29693v1/d_and_meta_d_vs_numTrials.svg" id="Sx2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/177;" width="429" height="177"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure S3: </span>Average <math id="Sx2.F3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math> (a) and meta-<math id="Sx2.F3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math> (b) versus number of trials. Each data point is the estimated <math id="Sx2.F3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math> and meta-<math id="Sx2.F3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math>, averaged over 20 repetitions, where each <math id="Sx2.F3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math> and meta-<math id="Sx2.F3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed with a given number of trials that is tuned in the x-axis. Error bars correspond to standard deviations. In panel (a), the error bars vanish because the simulation procedure deterministically set the type 1 response counts. The data has been generated using the function <span id="Sx2.F3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">exampleFit.m</span> from Ref. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fleming (2017)</a></cite>, available at <a href="https://github.com/smfleming/HMeta-d" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/smfleming/HMeta-d</a>, with the true <math id="Sx2.F3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math> and meta-<math id="Sx2.F3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29028^{\mathchar 560}</annotation></semantics></math>, indicated by a red horizontal dashed line in each panel, equal to 3.2 and 3 (i.e., very high type 1 sensitivity and high metacognitive efficiency), respectively. Type 1 criterion <math id="Sx2.F3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathchar 29027\mathchar 12349\mathchar 28720" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathchar 29027\mathchar 12349\mathchar 28720</annotation></semantics></math> and type 2 criteria are as follows: <span id="Sx2.F3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">c1 = [-2 -1.5 -1 -0.5]</span>, <span id="Sx2.F3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">c2 = [0.5 1 1.5 2]</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
